so Hogwarts Legacy drops not one but two  new clips this week they're very short  however it actually caused me to go back  and look at the previous two trailers  that we've gotten and I think I found  something that I haven't seen a lot of  people discussing so the first post is  here October 18th where will the grand  staircase lead you and a very nice shot  here during the daytime looking up at  the grand staircase you have the winged  boars over here on the right and you can  see a few portraits moving around kind  of here in the middle but other than  that not really a whole lot going on  here okay so then we have the second  post which also came on October 18th and  this one says the castle isn't only  meant to be explored during the day  super exciting here that they seem to be  really playing up the idea of us being  able to sneak around Hogwarts at night  they've actually talked about this a  number of times lately including when  they mentioned the restricted section of  the library as well as us being able to  sneak around the Forbidden Forest now  this shot here appears to be the exact  same one as before however it is set at  night so only a few differences here  first of all you have the flame names  over here on the right just above the  waned boars and now all of the lamps are  set to be on as well now I'm not sure if  this was intentional or if we're  supposed to read anything into it at all  but the second one the one that's set at  night there is no audio at all you just  hear the crackling of the fire whereas  the first one in the daytime actually  has music playing along with it so I  don't know if this means there's not  gonna be any music at night and maybe  instead we're focusing on the sounds of  the game and trying to sneak around you  know you're trying to be stealth so you  need to hear everything that's going on  I'm not sure but I did think it was an  interesting choice to see that we don't  have any nighttime music with this one  now during our recent live stream right  here on YouTube if you guys haven't  checked it out before we stream every  Tuesday night here we talk all things  Hogwarts Legacy and someone in my chat  actually mentioned hey did you notice  that none of the staircases are moving  here you know even though this is a  video clip we don't really see a whole  lot of movement there's a few things  kind of moving around with portraits and  we see one of those books flying around  again but in terms of the stairs they  aren't moving and anyone who's a fan of  Harry Potter Knows oh it's keeping on  the staircases they like to change we  read about this in the book of course we  see it in the movie and to be honest I  was never really a big fan of how it  worked in the movie I mean they kind of  just swivel all the way around it's  almost mechanical in nature rather than  feeling like it's actually magic however  we got a glimpse of what we thought this  was going to look like in the first  reveal trailer for Hogwarts Legacy take  a look at it here and I love this I  thought this was great I loved how it  appeared on screen and how everything  just sort of magically fell into place I  thought this felt way more like a magic  school than what we saw in the movies  however Troy Levitt former Hogwarts  Legacy Dev mentioned on an interview  with podcasts now that this was change  take a listen to this clip right here  from Troy here's what I'll say about the  grand staircase the early version that  you saw in the very first trailer uh is  different than I think what you end up  in the game so there you go there's  there's a small small reveal what we  discovered about making the the stairway  build up like that you know because it  was like you can see it in the film it  was building up underneath you well it's  too slow for players right players  didn't want to wait for the thing to  come around so we had to come up with a  fast faster way to make the grand  staircase do its thing that wouldn't  slow players down and that's a lot of  what you're doing when you're making a  game as you're like thinking oh that's  really cool what's it like when you  experience it dang it's a little too  slow or the timing's off well we need to  adjust it make it better you know that  it's a very iterative process it's  always responding you don't know what  you have in a game until you experience  it and and I think it's really important  for players and developers to recognize  that you can talk all day long about  what you think would be good but until  you actually get in and play it and  experience it you don't know what you  have so knowing this this caused me to  go back and look at the more recent  trailer and see if there were any shots  at all of the staircase do we see this  new animation that Troy is talking about  here because my first thought was ah  they probably made it just like the  movies but no that's not what they did  instead we do get a very very brief  Glimpse I think at least of how this is  going to work in the state of Play  trailer let's take a look right here and  you'll see that instead of them kind of  forming and just being all scattered as  they appear here now we have sort of  these individual pieces of the stair  sliding in from left to right there and  while I don't think I like it better  than the first option that we saw on  that original trailer I do like it  better than how the movies handled it so  again the state of Play trailer that's  been a while as well it'll be  interesting to see if they have changed  this yet again whenever we get another  update whenever we see a more extensive  trailer or who knows whenever we play  the final game but if you listen to that  full interview with Troy there are  definitely some interesting things to  think about in terms of how it actually  affects gameplay he mentions that the  first option was just too slow for  players and so they were having to get  there and then kind of wait on the  stairs to form instead of them just  naturally forming as the player walks  now in my head I'm like couldn't you  just speed that up but Troy knows way  more about making games than I do so I  trust him when he says this is something  that's difficult to pull off and now it  seems that we get a brief glimpse of  what they have came up with as the  solution in this other trailer and I can  certainly see how these would be able to  slide in much faster just kind of as  each stair appears here rather than  having all these individual pieces of  the stair kind of floating around and  forming now if you want to check out the  full stream where I break this down in  real time with my chat I do keep vods of  all those up right here on YouTube in  fact I'll put this most recent one right  here on the right side of your screen  now check it out as always thank you all  so much for watching I'll talk to you  again soon
 

